{"records":[{"id":"9rc2n4bkmv","title":"Functional interrogation of a SARS-CoV-2 host protein interactome identifies unique and shared coronavirus host factors. Hoffmann et al.","description":"The ongoing SARS-CoV-2 pandemic has devastated the global economy and claimed more than one million lives, presenting an urgent global health crisis. To identify host factors required for infection by SARS-CoV-2 and seasonal coronaviruses, we designed a focused high-coverage CRISPR-Cas9 library targeting 332 members of a recently published SARS-CoV-2 protein interactome. We leveraged the compact nature of this library to systematically screen SARS-CoV-2 at two physiologically relevant temperatures (33 ºC and 37 ºC) along with three related coronaviruses (HCoV-229E, HCoV-NL63, and HCoV-OC43), allowing us to probe this interactome at a much higher resolution relative to genome scale studies. This approach yielded several new insights, including unexpected virus-specific differences in Rab GTPase requirements and GPI anchor biosynthesis, as well as identification of multiple pan-coronavirus factors involved in cholesterol homeostasis. This coronavirus essentiality catalog could inform ongoing drug development efforts aimed at intercepting and treating COVID-19, and help prepare for future coronavirus outbreaks.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-25T19:01:19.445Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9rc2n4bkmv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9rc2n4bkmv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"JT","last_name":"Poirier","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9dk3rft75t","title":"Discovery and functional interrogation of SARS-CoV-2 RNA-host protein interactions. Flynn et al.","description":"Supplemental tables for the manuscript \"Discovery and functional interrogation of SARS-CoV-2 RNA-host protein interactions.\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-02-27T00:29:06.984Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9dk3rft75t","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9dk3rft75t"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Julia","last_name":"Belk","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","CRISPR","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9x47wzy8x7","title":"A study of \"Genome-wide CRISPR screens reveal host factors critical for SARS-CoV-2 infection\" by Wei et al. Cell 2020","description":"Identification of host genes essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection may reveal novel therapeutic targets and inform our understanding of COVID-19 pathogenesis. Here, we performed genome-wide CRISPR screens in Vero-E6 cells with SARS-CoV-2, MERS-CoV, bat coronavirus HKU5 expressing the SARS-CoV-1 spike, and VSV expressing the SARS-CoV-2 spike. Together this identifies potential therapeutic targets for SARS-CoV-2 and reveals SARS-lineage specific and pan-coronavirus host factors that regulate susceptibility to highly pathogenic coronaviruses.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-15T21:29:14.06Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9x47wzy8x7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9x47wzy8x7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Craig","last_name":"Wilen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR","Middle East Respiratory Syndrome-Related Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wxy2fkp5w8","title":"A study of \"Super-resolution proximity labeling reveals antiviral protein network and its structural changes against SARS-CoV-2 viral proteins\". Lee et al.","description":"SARS-CoV-2 replicates in human cells by interacting with host factors following infection. To understand the virus and host interactome, proximity, we introduce a super-resolution proximity labeling (SR-PL) method with “plug and playable” PL enzyme, TurboID-GBP (GFP binding protein) and we apply it for interactome mapping of SARS-CoV-2 ORF3a and M, which generates highly perturbed ER structures. Through SR-PL analysis of the biotinylated interactome, 224 and 272 peptides are robustly identified as ORF3a and M interactomes, respectively. Within the ORF3a interactome, RNF5 co-localizes with ORF3a and generates ubiquitin modifications of ORF3a that can be involved in protein degradation. We also observe that the SARS-CoV-2 infection rate is efficiently reduced by the overexpression of RNF5 in host cells. The interactome data obtains using the SR-PL method are presented in https://sarscov2.spatiomics.org. We hope that our method will contribute to revealing virus–host interactions of other viruses in an efficient manner.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:43:48.578Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wxy2fkp5w8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wxy2fkp5w8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yun-Bin","last_name":"Lee","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Minkyo","last_name":"Jung","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jeesoo","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Afandi","last_name":"Charles","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wanda","last_name":"Christ","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiwoong","last_name":"Kang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Myeong-Gyun","last_name":"Kang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chulhwan","last_name":"Kwak","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Klingström","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Anna","last_name":"Smed-Sörensen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jong-Seo","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"JiYoung","last_name":"Mun","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hyun-Woo","last_name":"Rhee","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/00fdzyk40","name":"Korea Health Industry Development Institute","grant_id":null},{"id":"https://ror.org/013aysd81","name":"National Research Foundation of Korea","grant_id":"NRF-2020K1A3A1A47110634, NRF-2021K2A9A1A01102293, NRF-2022R1A2B5B03001658, NRF-2022M3H9A2096199, 2022M3E5E8081185 to H.-W.R.; NRF-2022M3A9I2082294, NRF-2021R1A2C2009336 to J.-S.K."},{"id":"https://ror.org/055zd7d59","name":"Korea Brain Research Institute","grant_id":"23-BR-01-03"},{"id":"https://ror.org/00gjmje40","name":"Samsung Science and Technology Foundation (South Korea)","grant_id":"SSTF-BA2201-08"},{"id":"https://ror.org/04w3jy968","name":"Samsung (South Korea)","grant_id":"IO220819-02121-01"}],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4958h9zkty","title":"SARS-CoV-2 ncrRNA interactome","description":"A deep understanding of SARS-CoV-2-host interactions is crucial to developing effective therapeutics and addressing the threat of emerging coronavirus. The role of non-coding regions of viral RNA (ncrRNAs) has not been systematically scrutinized. We developed a method using MS2 affinity purification coupled with liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (MAMS) to systematically map the interactome of SARS-CoV-2 ncrRNA in Calu-3, Huh7, and HEK293T cells. Integration of the results defined the core ncrRNA-host protein interactomes. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-03-31T14:08:30.152Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4958h9zkty","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4958h9zkty"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Liuyiqi","last_name":"Jiang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"kfdxbzwhfj","title":"A study of \"Super-resolution proximity labeling reveals antiviral protein network and its structural changes against SARS-CoV-2 viral proteins\". Lee et al.","description":"SARS-CoV-2 replicates in human cells by interacting with host factors following infection. To understand the virus and host interactome, proximity, we introduce a super-resolution proximity labeling (SR-PL) method with “plug and playable” PL enzyme, TurboID-GBP (GFP binding protein) and we apply it for interactome mapping of SARS-CoV-2 ORF3a and M, which generates highly perturbed ER structures. Through SR-PL analysis of the biotinylated interactome, 224 and 272 peptides are robustly identified as ORF3a and M interactomes, respectively. Within the ORF3a interactome, RNF5 co-localizes with ORF3a and generates ubiquitin modifications of ORF3a that can be involved in protein degradation. We also observe that the SARS-CoV-2 infection rate is efficiently reduced by the overexpression of RNF5 in host cells. The interactome data obtains using the SR-PL method are presented in https://sarscov2.spatiomics.org. We hope that our method will contribute to revealing virus–host interactions of other viruses in an efficient manner.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-27T19:21:30.185Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kfdxbzwhfj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/kfdxbzwhfj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yun-Bin","last_name":"Lee","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Minkyo","last_name":"Jung","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jeesoo","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Afandi","last_name":"Charles","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wanda","last_name":"Christ","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiwoong","last_name":"Kang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Myeong-Gyun","last_name":"Kang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chulhwan","last_name":"Kwak","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Klingström","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jong-Seo","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"JiYoung","last_name":"Mun","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hyun-Woo","last_name":"Rhee","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"7bd5bhmhmz","title":"Genome-scale identification of SARS-CoV-2 and pan-coronavirus host factor networks. Schneider et al.","description":"The COVID-19 pandemic has claimed the lives of more than one million people worldwide. The causative agent, SARS-CoV-2, is a member of the Coronaviridae family, which are viruses that cause respiratory infections of varying severity. The cellular host factors and pathways co-opted by SARS- CoV-2 and other coronaviruses in the execution of their life cycles remain ill-defined. To develop an extensive compendium of host factors required for infection by SARS-CoV-2 and three seasonal coronaviruses (HCoV-OC43, HCoV-NL63, and HCoV-229E), we performed parallel genome-scale CRISPR knockout screens. These screens uncovered multiple host factors and pathways with pan- coronavirus and virus-specific functional roles, including major dependency on glycosaminoglycan biosynthesis, SREBP signaling, BMP signaling, and glycosylphosphatidylinositol biosynthesis, as well as a requirement for several poorly characterized proteins. We identified an absolute requirement for the VTT-domain containing protein TMEM41B for infection by SARS-CoV-2 and three seasonal coronaviruses. This human Coronaviridae host factor compendium represents a rich resource to develop new therapeutic strategies for acute COVID-19 and potential future coronavirus spillover events.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-12-03T09:15:53.589Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7bd5bhmhmz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7bd5bhmhmz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"JT","last_name":"Poirier","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"7fgg5452pr","title":"The SARS-CoV-2 interactome","description":"SARS-CoV-2 is an RNA virus whose success as a pathogen relies on its abilities to repurpose host RNA-binding proteins (RBPs) and to evade antiviral RBPs. To uncover the SARS-CoV-2 RNA interactome, we here develop a robust ribonucleoprotein (RNP) capture protocol and identify 109 host factors that directly bind to SARS-CoV-2 RNAs. Applying RNP capture on another coronavirus HCoV-OC43 revealed evolutionarily conserved interactions between coronaviral RNAs and host proteins. Transcriptome analyses and knockdown experiments delineated 17 antiviral RBPs including ZC3HAV1, TRIM25, PARP12, and SHFL and 8 proviral RBPs such as EIF3D and CSDE1 which are responsible for co-opting multiple steps of the mRNA life cycle. This also led to the identification of LARP1, a downstream target of the mTOR signaling pathway, as an antiviral host factor that interacts with the SARS-CoV-2 RNAs. Overall, this study provides a comprehensive list of RBPs regulating coronaviral replication and opens new avenues for therapeutic interventions.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-05-07T07:11:04.995Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7fgg5452pr","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7fgg5452pr"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sungyul","last_name":"Lee","orcid":"0000-0003-3207-1199"},{"first_name":"Young-suk","last_name":"Lee","orcid":"0000-0003-0220-9951"},{"first_name":"Yeon","last_name":"Choi","orcid":"0000-0003-4983-6573"},{"first_name":"Aheyon","last_name":"Son","orcid":"0000-0001-7945-3851"},{"first_name":"Youngran","last_name":"Park","orcid":"0000-0002-8621-1399"},{"first_name":"Kyung-Min","last_name":"Lee","orcid":"0000-0002-1373-5407"},{"first_name":"Jeesoo","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jong-Seo","last_name":"Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-8909-8440"},{"first_name":"V. Narry","last_name":"Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-3213-4965"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Proteomics","RNA","Interactome","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"kjs2wnncjs","title":"\"Virus-host interactome and proteomic survey of PBMCs from COVID-19 patients reveal potential virulence factors influencing SARS-CoV-2 pathogenesis\" by Li et al.","description":"Supplementary Table S1-S4 for the paper entitled \"Virus-host interactome and proteomic survey of PBMCs from COVID-19 patients reveal potential virulence factors influencing SARS-CoV-2 pathogenesis\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-07-14T04:12:35.355Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kjs2wnncjs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/kjs2wnncjs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Qiming","last_name":"Liang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chao","last_name":"Peng","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tongyu","last_name":"Zhu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zhenshan","last_name":"Liu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gcdpsxd6d5","title":"RNAi screening using HK-2 cells: insights into the roles of soluble ACE2 in SARS-CoV-2 infection. Yeung et al","description":"Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) can cause acute respiratory disease and multiorgan failure. Finding human host factors that are essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection could facilitate the formulation of treatment strategies. Using a human kidney cell line—HK-2—that is highly susceptible to SARS-CoV-2, we performed a genome-wide RNAi screening and identified virus dependency factors (VDFs), which play regulatory roles in biological pathways linked to clinical manifestations of SARS-CoV-2 infection. Importantly, we discovered an overlooked role of a secretory form of SARS-CoV-2 receptor, soluble angiotensin converting enzyme 2 (sACE2), in SARS-CoV-2 infection. Further investigations revealed that SARS-CoV-2 exploits receptor-mediated endocytosis through interaction between its spike with sACE2 or sACE2-vasopressin via AT1 or AVPR1B, respectively. Our identification of new VDFs and the regulatory effect of sACE2 on SARS-CoV-2 infection shed new insights into pathogenesis and cell entry mechanism of SARS-CoV-2 as well as potential treatment strategies for COVID-19.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-02-22T23:41:07.557Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gcdpsxd6d5","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gcdpsxd6d5"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Man Lung","last_name":"Yeung","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Screening","RNA Knockdown"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":145997,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":296,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":145997,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":145205,"restricted":72,"embargoed":720},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":3567},{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2315},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":703},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":474},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":456},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":440},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":423},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":394},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":326},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":275}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":143335},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1908},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":186},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":141},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":80},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":66},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":58},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":44},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":32},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":27}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":3099},{"id":"ecb64011-71f0-5223-b4e4-4d27d5f51d83","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid Centro de Biologia Molecular Severo Ochoa","count":2347},{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":532},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":409},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":361}]}}